.MARINE...
(Today through Sunday)
Issued at 939 AM PDT Tue Oct 6 2026

High pressure off the Pacific Northwest Coast and low pressure
near Southern California will maintain gentle to moderate
northerly breezes through Thursday. Northerly breezes will then
increase strong to very strong Friday into Saturday, bringing
widespread hazardous conditions for small craft. Frequent gale
force gusts are likely across the northern waters during this
time. Moderate seas will prevail through Thursday, building to
become rough to very rough Friday into Saturday.

