.FIRE WEATHER...
Issued at 456 AM PDT Tue Oct 6 2026

Maximum and minimum temperatures 10 to 20 degrees above normal
across the interior with a compressed marine layer at the coast
will persist through Thursday. Widespread poor minimum relative
humidity is expected across the interior with little-to-no
recovery for the higher terrain. Active thermal belting and prolonged
burn periods will continue across the higher terrain. Winds
remain the limiting factor, with diurnal winds prevailing except
for light northerly/offshore flow overnight across the higher
terrain. ERC values are forecast to reach near records during the
next seven days from the hot and dry conditions. An inside slider
like pattern succeeding this heat event will likely keep elevated
fire weather conditions around.

